UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Deduct the full $20,000 net loss against ordinary income","Deduct $3,000 against ordinary income and carry forward the remainder","Carry back 3 years and forward 5 years as a short-term capital loss","Carry forward indefinitely with no current-year deduction allowed"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 1212(a), corporations carry net capital losses back 3 years and forward 5 years, treating carryovers as short-term capital losses regardless of original character. IRC Section 1211(a) prohibits corporations from deducting net capital losses against ordinary income.
Wrong (A): Corporations cannot deduct capital losses against ordinary income under IRC Section 1211(a); this rule applies only to individuals (up to $3,000 under Section 1211(b)).
Wrong (B): The $3,000 annual deduction against ordinary income is an individual taxpayer rule under Section 1211(b), not available to corporations.
Wrong (D): Corporate capital loss carryforwards expire after 5 years under Section 1212(a); they do not carry forward indefinitely.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2802;

-- Q2809: C Corporations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["E&P decreases by $100,000 with no gain recognized on distribution","E&P decreases by $40,000 based solely on the property''s adjusted basis","E&P increases by $60,000 for gain recognized but decreases only by $40,000","E&P increases by $60,000 then decreases by $100,000 for a net $40,000 decrease"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 311(b), a corporation distributing appreciated property recognizes gain equal to the excess of FMV over basis ($60,000), increasing E&P. E&P is then reduced by the FMV distributed ($100,000), yielding a net $40,000 decrease.
Wrong (A): E&P is not simply reduced by FMV; the corporation must first recognize gain under Section 311(b), which increases E&P before the distribution reduces it.
Wrong (B): Using only the adjusted basis ignores both the gain recognition under Section 311(b) and the FMV-based E&P reduction.
Wrong (C): This choice correctly recognizes the $60,000 gain but incorrectly limits the E&P decrease to $40,000; the reduction equals the full FMV of $100,000.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2809;

-- Q2826: S Corporations [medium/L2]
