UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["No relief is available and the S election is permanently terminated","The IRS may grant inadvertent termination relief treating the election as continuing","Holly may immediately re-elect S status without any waiting period required","Holly must wait five years before it is eligible to re-elect S status"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1362(f), if the IRS determines that a termination was inadvertent and the corporation promptly corrects the disqualifying event, the IRS may treat the S election as if it had never terminated. Holly corrected the issue by having the alien sell the stock back.
Wrong (A): Section 1362(f) specifically provides a relief mechanism for inadvertent terminations, so the election is not automatically and permanently lost.
Wrong (C): Immediate re-election is not available; if relief is denied, the corporation must wait five years under Section 1362(g) or obtain IRS consent.
Wrong (D): The five-year waiting period under Section 1362(g) applies when relief is denied, but the question asks about available relief, which Section 1362(f) provides.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2826;

-- Q2865: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["That the CPA made a material error in the financial statements filed","That the CPA failed to follow generally accepted auditing standards throughout","That the plaintiff suffered financial harm from reliance on the CPA''s work","Misrepresentation, scienter, intent to induce reliance, actual reliance, and damages"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under common law fraud (Restatement (Second) of Torts Section 525), five elements must be proven: a material misrepresentation of fact, scienter (knowledge of falsity or reckless disregard), intent to induce reliance, justifiable reliance by the plaintiff, and resulting damages. All five must be established.
Wrong (A): A material error alone is insufficient; fraud requires proof of scienter and the other elements beyond mere mistake.
Wrong (B): Failure to follow GAAS supports a negligence claim, not fraud; fraud requires knowing or reckless misrepresentation.
Wrong (C): Financial harm is only one element; without proof of scienter and intent to induce reliance, a fraud claim fails.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2865;

-- Q2872: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The client''s general ledger maintained during the tax year","The CPA''s audit workpapers prepared in the ordinary course of business","A litigation-anticipation memo analyzing the client''s legal exposure","The CPA''s signed engagement letter establishing the professional relationship"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
