UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["File a UCC-1 financing statement within 20 days of the debtor''s receipt","Record the purchase-money security interest with the county recorder''s office","Obtain a court order specifically granting superpriority over prior lienholders","Perfect before delivery and send authenticated notice to the prior-perfected party"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under UCC Section 9-324(b), a PMSI in inventory achieves superpriority only if the holder perfects before the debtor receives the inventory and sends authenticated notification to the prior-perfected secured party. Both steps are required for inventory PMSIs.
Wrong (A): The 20-day perfection grace period applies to PMSIs in equipment under Section 9-324(a), not inventory; inventory PMSIs must be perfected before the debtor receives possession.
Wrong (B): UCC Article 9 security interests are perfected by filing with the state filing office, not recorded with the county recorder.
Wrong (C): Superpriority is established by statute through perfection and notice, not by court order.$EXPL$
