-- Q4799: Government Regulation of Business [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Provide a workplace free from recognized hazards likely to cause death or serious harm","Purchase personal health insurance coverage for all current employees on the payroll","Guarantee that zero workplace injuries will occur during each calendar year","Allow employees to refuse any assigned task they personally consider unpleasant"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under 29 U.S.C. Section 654(a)(1), the OSHA general duty clause requires employers to furnish a workplace free from recognized hazards that are causing or likely to cause death or serious physical harm. This applies regardless of specific OSHA standards.
Wrong (B): OSHA addresses workplace safety conditions, not health insurance; health insurance requirements fall under the Affordable Care Act for applicable large employers.
Wrong (C): OSHA requires employers to address recognized hazards, but does not impose a zero-injury guarantee, which would be an impossible standard.
Wrong (D): Employees have a limited right to refuse imminently dangerous work, but OSHA does not grant the right to refuse tasks merely because they are unpleasant.$EXPL$
